        ("Where should I look first when a Spark job is slow?", "Open the slowest stage and ask which bucket it is: reading too much, shuffling, computing, spilling, one straggler task, or waiting. Fix the dominant bucket. Tuning a small bucket first rarely changes the total."),
        ("Is more parallelism always faster?", "No. Parallelism helps until each piece is so small that starting it costs more than doing it. Aim for partitions of roughly 100 to 200 MB, and watch for tiny tasks and tiny output files."),
        ("Why do small files hurt so much?", "Every file costs an open, a metadata lookup and a task slot before any data moves. Ten thousand 1 MB files do far more overhead than ten 1 GB files holding the same data."),
        ("Why does a low-cardinality column compress so well?", "A column with five distinct values can be stored as a short code per row plus a five-entry dictionary, then run-length encoded. Unique values like ids have no repeats to exploit."),
        ("When does an embedded engine like DuckDB beat a cluster?", "When data fits on one machine. A cluster pays job start-up, planning and shuffle cost on every action. For small and medium data on one node, that fixed overhead dominates, and a single-process engine avoids it."),
        ("Are the time and size numbers on this page measured?", "No. They are orders of magnitude to build intuition. Measure your own job with the engine's query profile before deciding."),
